// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// i18n.js -- the English/French translation table and lookup functions,
// physically split out of withdrawal_strategy_JP.html (Priority 16,
// Phase 3).
//
// uiLang (the current language, 'en'/'fr'), the full I18N string table, and
// the two pure lookup functions that read them (t(), bt()) all moved
// verbatim. None of these three touch the DOM directly -- they're a plain
// data table plus two lookup functions -- so, like engine.js and state.js
// before them, this is a zero-behavior-change physical move only.
//
// What did NOT move: applyI18n() (sweeps the DOM applying t() to every
// [data-i18n*] element) and setUiLang() (the EN/FR toggle handler -- reads
// the DOM, persists via _stateSet, re-renders) both touch the DOM directly,
// so both stay in the main file, same reasoning as every other UI-facing
// function Phase 2/3 left behind.
//
// Known cross-file dependency (harmless, documented rather than "fixed" --
// same spirit as the two gaps Phase 2 documented in engine.js): engine.js's
// _cppQppLabelDisp() reads uiLang directly (to pick the French RRQ/RPC
// acronym) with no override guard, same as every other reference to it
// across the app -- it's an ordinary shared global by the time anything
// actually calls that function, exactly like every other cross-file
// reference in this app, so nothing breaks; noted here for completeness.
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// ── i18n (English/French UI toggle) ─────────────────────────────────────────
// Decisions locked in with JP 2026-09-13 (see ROADMAP.md): a permanent EN/FR
// toggle (never a one-way replace), full surface-text scope including the
// Help tab, standard Quebec financial acronyms (REER/FERR/CELI/RRQ/SV/FRV)
// rather than literal translations, and code/comments/variable names staying
// English always -- only what a user actually sees in the rendered UI goes
// through this layer. Built as a 5-phase batch; this is Phase 1 (toggle
// infrastructure + Profile + Income/Budget tabs). Every I18N key covers BOTH
// languages up front even for tabs not yet in scope (e.g. the nav bar's own
// tab labels) so cross-references made by an already-translated tab (e.g.
// Profile's helper text naming "the Retirement Income tab") read correctly
// today and don't need to be revisited when that other tab's own body copy
// is translated in a later phase.
//
// uiLang starts at the plain default here (mirroring _currencyShortForm's
// own pattern just above) and is overwritten from saved state inside the
// synchronous restore IIFE further down the file, alongside every other
// Profile-tab setting -- NOT here at top-level script scope, since _stateGet
// itself isn't safe to call until the "Unified app-state storage" section
// below (and its _appState `let`) has actually executed.
let uiLang = 'en';

// Every user-facing string lives here, keyed by a short stable name. Add to
// this table, never scatter a second EN/FR pair somewhere else -- t() is the
// only lookup path so future maintenance (a wording tweak, a new language)
// touches exactly one place per string.
